      "problem": "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = -3 a_n,\\qquad a_1 = 2,\\qquad n \\geq 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-3{a}_{1}=-3(2)=-6 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-3{a}_{2}=-3(-6)=18 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-3{a}_{3}=-3(18)=-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a_4 = -54.$",
